# Almost everything Android Studio writes into .idea/ is machine specific -
# gradle.xml records your Gradle JDK path, misc.xml your SDK, workspace.xml
# your window layout and open tabs. None of that should follow the repository.
#
# The exception is runConfigurations/, which is the supported way to share Run
# and Debug entries with everyone who opens the project. Those are committed
# on purpose, so this file is an allowlist rather than a list of exclusions:
# anything Studio invents later is ignored by default instead of turning up
# as an unexpected diff.

/*
!/.gitignore
!/runConfigurations/
